  "requires_note": "Measured by the internal capability test (plan 13.21.3): ntm drives sessions through tmux (tmux is present here, so this one is met); ft's core observation needs the WezTerm mux, and ft's own status says \"WezTerm bridge CLI not found in PATH\"; cass-memory's own diagnostic reports the companion 'cass' CLI is unavailable. Only requirements the test actually measured are declared: blockers that are not a component, an executable or a variable - a .beads directory for br/bv, project initialisation for slb, a daemon plus root for sbh's reclamation, and an API key whose variable name is not evidenced for cass - are deliberately absent rather than guessed. ee's EE_SERVE_TOKEN is a requirement of its serve mode, so it belongs on a future service entry, not on the package."
